  obtainNote: "\u0E40\u0E0A\u0E1F\u0E44\u0E17\u0E22 \u0E09\u0E1A\u0E31\u0E1A\u0E41\u0E23\u0E01
    \u0E40\u0E21\u0E19\u0E39\u0E08\u0E32\u0E19\u0E40\u0E14\u0E35\u0E22\u0E27\u0E22\u0E2D\u0E14\u0E19\u0E34\u0E22\u0E21"
  mailShopLevel: 1
  mailReputation: 50
  chef: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 9027734d34a03bb43947e2332bd51243, type: 2}
  letterBody: 'Dear young owner,


    My niece showed me the reviews of your little
    restaurant on her phone. A countryside shop serving food from six countries?
    I had to write.


    I''m Malai. I''ve run a kitchen in Bangkok for thirty years,
    but I started at my mother''s street stall, frying holy basil pork for taxi drivers
    at two in the morning. They had no time, only hunger, and this dish never let
    them down.


    Hot wok, lots of garlic and chili, and the basil goes in last.
    A fried egg on top, crispy at the edges. That''s the whole secret.


    Someone
    who cooks for strangers deserves a good everyday dish.'
